# Clarinete: Chowning §IV uses N1:N2 with the carrier at the fundamental and
# the modulator at the same frequency to favour odd harmonics. I≈24 semitones
# gives β = (2^(24/12)−1)/1 = 3 → 3 sidebands of significant magnitude, which
# yields the characteristic hollow/reed timbre. Soft attack, high sustain.
1	InstrumentFM	ADSR_A=0.08; ADSR_D=0.10; ADSR_S=0.80; ADSR_R=0.15; N1=1; N2=1; I=24;
